;; clj-kondo export for day8/re-frame2-fresco: macro-shape analysis only.
;;
;; A consumer picks this up with clj-kondo's ordinary dependency import —
;; nothing here is re-frame2-specific plumbing:
;;
;;   clj-kondo --lint "$(clojure -Spath)" --dependencies --copy-configs
;;
;; run from a project root where a `.clj-kondo/` directory already exists
;; (without one it copies nothing and still exits 0). It copies this export
;; to `.clj-kondo/imports/day8/re-frame2-fresco/`, where clj-kondo loads it
;; with no `:config-paths` entry. See README.md beside this file.
;;
;; The hooks give `defview`, `event` and `defhost` their `defn`, `fn` and
;; `def` shapes, so kondo's ordinary analysis applies: names resolve,
;; destructured props are neither unresolved nor unused, arities are checked.
;; No custom findings ship — behavior is the runtime's law, refused loudly at
;; its execution boundary, not re-derived in a lint layer.
{;; `re-frame.fresco.native` is two React hooks, `use-sub` and
 ;; `use-frame` — ordinary functions, so they need neither a `:lint-as`
 ;; nor a hook.
 :hooks
 {:analyze-call
  {re-frame.fresco/defview hooks.re-frame.fresco/defview
   re-frame.fresco/event   hooks.re-frame.fresco/event
   re-frame.fresco/defhost hooks.re-frame.fresco/defhost}}}
